==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 0.07~0.33 seconds<sup>2f~10f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Sir Seal]]s spawn, delay 6~16.67 seconds<sup>180f~500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Metal Hippoe]]s spawn after 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*10 [[Metal Hippoe]]s spawn after 166.67 seconds<sup>5,000f</sup>, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
*10 [[H. Nah]]s spawn after 233.33 seconds<sup>7,000f</sup>, delay 20~33.33 seconds<sup>600f~1,000f</sup>.
*10 [[H. Nah]]s spawn after 933.33 seconds<sup>28,000f</sup>, delay 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Sir Metal Seal]] spawns as the boss.

==Strategy==
Use any Cat that has the ability to do a [[Critical Hit]] to deal with Sir Metal Seal. Use [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] to deal with the regular Seals.

Sir Metal Seal is unstoppable if you do not bring Cats that can do Critical Hits, so bringing units such as [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Major Space Cat]] and [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] is highly recommended (only True Form outranges him). If you happen to own any units obtained through beating [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]] stages, they're all anti-Metal crowd-controllers and help immensely with stopping Sir Metal Seal's advance. Using [[Moneko (Special Cat)|Miss Moneko]] is recommended if you can keep Sir Metal Seal in place, since she does almost enough damage to instantly kill him through a Critical Hit, though only barely outranges him. Additionally, if you own [[Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Neneko]], she has an amazing [[Cat Combo]] with Moneko.

You shouldn't have to worry about the H. Nah spam under normal circumstances, since you'll typically be able to kill the Sir Metal Seal before the four minute time limit is up.

